    <string name="toggle_usage_log">Enable diagnostic logs</string>
    <string name="hint_usage_log">Writes a log file to Downloads and to logcat. Turn off before handing the app to someone else.</string>
    <string name="label_canvas_quality">Canvas quality</string>
    <string name="canvas_quality_normal">Normal (2×)</string>
    <string name="canvas_quality_perf">Performance (1.4×)</string>
    <string name="hint_canvas_quality">Performance uses less memory and reduces lag on slower phones, but leaves less room to zoom out beyond the visible page. No effect in kid mode (zoom is already locked there).</string>
    <string name="label_melange_experiment">Color mixing (experimental)</string>
    <string name="melange_experiment_off">Off</string>
    <string name="melange_experiment_protection">Anti-revert protection</string>
    <string name="melange_experiment_rayon">Tighter radius</string>
    <string name="melange_experiment_retour_lent">Slower revert</string>
    <string name="hint_melange_experiment">The ball keeps falling back into the screen\'s dominant color as soon as it touches it again. 3 approaches to compare in real use, none settled yet: Protection ignores the color just left for a short while, Tighter radius makes the ball less sensitive to its surroundings, Slower revert only slows the pull back toward the color just left. Off = current behavior, unchanged.</string>
    <string name="label_tilt_response_experiment">Tilt response (experimental)</string>
    <string name="tilt_response_current">Current</string>
    <string name="tilt_response_lineaire">Linear</string>
    <string name="tilt_response_adouci">Softened</string>
    <string name="hint_tilt_response_experiment">External tester feedback: the ball feels slow and heavy to get moving. The default ball\'s squared tilt curve barely responds to a normal tilt. 2 approaches to compare in real use: Linear reacts immediately to any tilt (ignores each ball\'s squared-curve setting), Softened keeps the progressive feel but far less flattened at everyday tilt angles. Current = today\'s behavior (respects each ball\'s own setting), unchanged.</string>
    <string name="label_mix_vivid_experiment">Color mixing vividness (experimental)</string>
    <string name="mix_vivid_current">Current</string>
    <string name="mix_vivid_chroma">Boosted chroma</string>
    <string name="mix_vivid_teinte">Hue blend</string>
    <string name="hint_mix_vivid_experiment">The realistic pigment mixing (Kubelka-Munk) can turn muddy brown on complementary colors, like real paint does. 2 approaches to compare in real use: Boosted chroma keeps the same mix but pushes saturation back up afterward, Hue blend drops realism entirely for a pure hue fade (never brown, but no longer "real paint"). Current = today\'s behavior, unchanged.</string>
